WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.080
This video covers Sentinel.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.960
When a recording is
processed, Sentinel can flag

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.230
moments of confrontational
client behavior for later review.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.510
A flagged encounter shows a
safety alert above the note.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.440
Click a marked moment to hear it in the

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.365
original audio, and check
it against the transcript.

00:00:16.775 --> 00:00:20.365
The flagged encounter is preserved
beyond the standard retention window.

00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:22.695
You can fold the alert away on screen.

00:00:22.695 --> 00:00:24.125
That doesn't remove the flag.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.550
Open Messages and choose
the Flagged filter.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.280
It shows client threads linked
to flagged encounters, so

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.030
you can open the visit before you answer.

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:36.683
A flag is a reason to review the
recording, not proof of what happened.

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:40.293
Sentinel only analyzes audio
you chose to record, and it

00:00:40.293 --> 00:00:43.963
does not contact clients, authorities,
or anyone outside your practice.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:47.243
Your team's own safety and
escalation policies still apply.
